  "usage_note": "A **sentence** is complete and can stand alone; it usually has a subject and a verb (*She left early.*), though an order may have no stated subject (*Sit down.*). A **phrase** is a small group of words without its own subject and verb (*in the morning*). A **clause** has a subject and a verb but may be only part of a sentence (*when she left*).",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "I wrote three phrases about my weekend.",
      "correct": "I wrote three sentences about my weekend.",
      "note": "Complete statements are **sentences**; a **phrase** is only part of one, such as *on Saturday morning*."
    }
  ],
